{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TowerGeometricSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.TowerGeometricSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Module.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uniform_bound_not_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uniform_bound_not_const","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L176-L188","doc":"The gap between the two results above, as a statement rather than a comment:\na uniform bound does NOT give level-independence.  Witnessed by an alternating\nresidual, which is uniformly bounded by `1` and not constant.\n\n(Still true and still the right statement — but note the ACTUAL residual is not\nmerely non-constant, it is `lam ^ n`; see `towerSum_iterated`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.leadingMode_lam_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.leadingMode_lam_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L168-L174","doc":"At the leading mode `[1]_q = 1`, so `λ_1 = ℏ_q / L_q²`, and `λ_1 = 1` pins\n`L_q² = ℏ_q`.  Stated on `L_q²` so no square root is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated_eq_simple_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated_eq_simple_iff","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L155-L166","doc":"**The implemented factor `1/(1 - ℏ_q²)` is the `lam = 1` member of that\nfamily, and only that one.**  So adopting it is adopting `λ_k = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_iterated","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L138-L153","doc":"**The tower of an ITERATED residual.**  With `Δ^{(n)}` the `n`-th iterate,\neigenvalue `lam ^ n`, the tower is geometric in `ℏ_q² · lam`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_le_of_uniform_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_le_of_uniform_bound","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L91-L109","doc":"**What the corpus actually proves buys you: a bound, not the value.**\nGiven only `|Δ^{(n)}| ≤ M` uniformly in `n` — which is exactly\n`delta_max_uniform_bound` — the geometric expression bounds the tower's\nmagnitude termwise.\n\nStated termwise rather than on the `tsum` so it carries no summability\nhypothesis: each partial sum is dominated, which is the honest content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.towerSum_of_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.towerSum_of_const","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L67-L89","doc":"**The identity `tower_summed` uses.**  A tower `Σ_n ℏ_q^{2n} · Δ` whose\nresidual is LEVEL-INDEPENDENT sums to `Δ / (1 - ℏ_q²)`.\n\nThis is where the `1/(1 - ℏ_q²)` in `qbeta_e0.tower_summed` comes from: the\n`ℏ_q^{2n}` is the brane tower's structural grading, and `Δ^{(n)} = Δ` is the\nhypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_sq_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_sq_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L51-L65","doc":"At `q > 1` the tower ratio `ℏ_q²` is in `[0, 1)`, so the grading converges.\nAt the substrate pin `q₀ ≈ 1.11` this gives `ℏ_q² ≈ 0.0098`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/TowerGeometricSum.lean#L48-L49","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 - 1/q`, the substrate deformation parameter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}